{"entry_id": "2025-02-20-bracken-manufacturing-case-study-CS-01", "source_file": "2025-02-20_Bracken_Manufacturing_Case_Study.docx", "source_type": "docx", "report_date": "2025-02-20", "section": "case_study", "object_name": "Bracken Manufacturing Shop-Floor Rollout", "pic": ["Elena Rossi", "Priya Patel"], "client": "Bracken Manufacturing Co.", "bo": "—", "activity": "Bracken Manufacturing Co. piloted Meridian Access Platform on 400 shop-floor tablets at its Denver plant during a six-week evaluation completed in Q1 2025; device provisioning time dropped from 42 minutes to 6 minutes per unit, attributed to the bulk certificate renewal feature shipped in Device Enrollment Service v1.4. These results directly informed the company-wide 3,800-unit rollout proposal that remained under review as of late February 2025.", "activity_sha256": "17e78e72bc022462d44b3bc6e4e94a8c61a8ee1e08cba68dfe8543974fcc8d84", "raw_ref": "_kb/md/2025-02-20-bracken-manufacturing-case-study.md#2025-02-20-bracken-manufacturing-case-study-CS-01", "category": "Manufacturing", "subcategory": "Discrete Manufacturing", "category_conf": "stated/high"}
